From edd74ba804f004bc0e59a07490261681acc0e299 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:46:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] libcamera: software_isp: Gather focus statistics

Contrast detection autofocus needs a measure of the image sharpness over
parts of the frame. Add a grid of 8x6 focus regions to the software ISP
statistics. For each region, accumulate the squared difference between
the green values of horizontally adjacent samples, along with the sum of
the green values and the number of samples, so that the IPA can
normalise the measurement for brightness.

The statistics are gathered in the existing line functions, which are
shared by the CPU and GPU debayering paths. The line functions now take
the line number relative to the statistics window to locate the grid
row.

Add a unit test that checks the region values on synthetic frames.

[backport: adapted to v0.7.2, which predates commit 7ebae537
 ("libcamera: software_isp: Exclude saturated pixels from AWB
 statistics"), and extended to the quad Bayer statistics of the
 postmarketOS downstream patch]

Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
